      </section>

      <section class="examples-section kst-image-split" aria-labelledby="remote-title">
        <div>
          <h2 id="remote-title">Remote developers, support queues, and product launches</h2>
          <p>Software teams schedule around the human clock for stakeholder calls and the technical clock used in logs, cron jobs, queues, and deployments. Keep machine events in UTC when possible, then publish human-facing notes in KST and Eastern Time.</p>
          <p>For global product launches, separate the launch time, code freeze, support staffing window, and executive checkpoint. A single KST timestamp can map to different Eastern calendar labels depending on daylight saving time.</p>
        </div>
        <figure class="kst-wide-figure reveal">
