      <section class="examples-section" aria-labelledby="markets-title">
        <h2 id="markets-title">Stock market and investor scheduling</h2>
        <p>Korean market news can reach Eastern readers outside normal U.S. office hours. Earnings updates, exchange notices, investor calls, supplier announcements, and macroeconomic releases may be discussed in one country while the other country is on a different calendar date. Analysts should identify which market session the timestamp belongs to before drawing conclusions.</p>
        <p>A Korean manufacturer may post a disclosure at 8 AM KST. In New York, that can be the previous evening with a different hour by season. Global announcements should carry the official KST timestamp, the Eastern equivalent, and a UTC reference.</p>
      </section>

